# 🛕 Jagannath Temple Donation System — v11.0 (MongoDB Edition)

> **Backend converted from MySQL / SQLAlchemy → MongoDB / PyMongo**
> All API endpoints, frontend JavaScript, and application flow are **identical**.
> Only the database layer has changed.

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
PROJECT_TEMPLE-DONATION - Mongodb/
│
├── main.py              ← FastAPI app — all API routes (~1 000 lines)
├── database.py          ← MongoClient + get_db() + get_next_id() + indexes
├── models.py            ← Row wrapper + collection constants + doc builders
├── schemas.py           ← Pydantic v2 request/response models (unchanged)
├── faq_routes.py        ← FAQ CRUD sub-router (mounted at /faq)
├── seed.py              ← Seeds zodiac, gotra, tithis, calendar data
├── seed_faq.py          ← Seeds FAQ content
├── requirements.txt     ← Python dependencies
├── .env                 ← Secrets (never commit to Git)
├── .env.example         ← Template — copy to .env and fill in values
├── CODE_STRUCTURE.py    ← Full annotated code-structure reference
│
├── templates/
│   └── index.html       ← Multi-step frontend UI (unchanged)
│
└── static/
    ├── app.js           ← All frontend logic — fetch() calls only (unchanged)
    └── style.css        ← All styling (unchanged)
```

> ✅ No `Database.sql` needed — MongoDB creates collections automatically on first write.

---

## ⚡ Quick Start

### Option A — Local Setup (Windows / Linux / Mac)

```bash
# 1. Clone / extract the project
cd "PROJECT_TEMPLE-DONATION - Mongodb"

# 2. Create & activate virtual environment
python -m venv venv
# Windows:
venv\Scripts\activate
# Linux / Mac:
source venv/bin/activate

# 3. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 4. Copy .env.example → .env and fill in your values
cp .env.example .env

# 5. Ensure MongoDB is running (see MongoDB Setup section below)

# 6. Seed master data (run once)
python seed.py
python seed_faq.py

# 7. Start the server
uvicorn main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
```

Open → **http://localhost:8000**
Swagger API Docs → **http://localhost:8000/docs**

---

### Option B — Docker (single container, MongoDB + FastAPI)

```bash
# Build
docker build -t temple-donation .

# Run (creates named volume for data persistence)
docker run -d \
  -p 8000:8000 \
  -v temple_data:/data/db \
  -e DB_NAME=temple_donation \
  -e SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com \
  -e SMTP_PASSWORD=your_app_password \
  --name temple-app \
  temple-donation

# Seed data (first time only)
docker exec -it temple-app python seed.py
docker exec -it temple-app python seed_faq.py
```

Open → **http://localhost:8000**

---

## 🍃 MongoDB Setup (Local)

### Windows

1. Download from: https://www.mongodb.com/try/download/community
2. Choose **Windows → MSI installer**
3. ✅ Check **"Install MongoDB as a Service"** during setup
4. Start:
   ```cmd
   net start MongoDB
   ```
5. Verify:
   ```cmd
   mongosh
   # Should show: Connecting to: mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017
   ```

### Linux (Ubuntu/Debian)

```bash
curl -fsSL https://www.mongodb.org/static/pgp/server-7.0.asc | \
  sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/mongodb-server-7.0.gpg

echo "deb [ arch=amd64,arm64 signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/mongodb-server-7.0.gpg ] \
  https://repo.mongodb.org/apt/ubuntu jammy/mongodb-org/7.0 multiverse" | \
  sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/mongodb-org-7.0.list

sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y mongodb-org
sudo systemctl start mongod
sudo systemctl enable mongod
```

### Mac

```bash
brew tap mongodb/brew
brew install mongodb-community@7.0
brew services start mongodb/brew/mongodb-community
```

