## 🔍 Useful MongoDB Queries

```js
// Switch database
use temple_donation

// List all collections
show collections

// Count donors
db.donors.countDocuments()

// Find donor by phone
db.donors.findOne({ whatsapp_number: "+919876543210" })

// All seva donations for a donor
db.seva_donations.find({ donor_id: 1 }).pretty()

// Find by receipt number
db.seva_donations.findOne({ receipt_no: "JGN-20260501-3742" })

// All active sevas
db.seva.find({ is_active: 1 }).pretty()

// View auto-increment counters
db.counters.find().pretty()

// All users (hide password hash)
db.users.find({}, { hashed_password: 0 }).pretty()

// Check indexes on donors collection
db.donors.getIndexes()

// Search donors by name (case-insensitive)
db.donors.find({ first_name: { $regex: "ram", $options: "i" } })
```

---

## 🆚 MySQL → MongoDB Migration Summary

| Aspect | MySQL (old) | MongoDB (new) |
|---|---|---|
| Driver | `sqlalchemy` + `pymysql` | `pymongo` |
| Schema definition | ORM models | Collection constants + `Row` wrapper |
| ID generation | `AUTO_INCREMENT` | `counters` collection + `get_next_id()` |
| Read one | `db.query(Model).filter().first()` | `db["col"].find_one({...})` |
| Read many | `db.query(Model).all()` | `list(db["col"].find({...}))` |
| Insert | `db.add(obj); db.commit()` | `db["col"].insert_one(doc)` |
| Update | `obj.field = val; db.commit()` | `db["col"].update_one({}, {"$set":{...}})` |
| Delete | `db.delete(obj); db.commit()` | `db["col"].delete_one({...})` |
| Cascade delete | FK `ON DELETE CASCADE` | Explicit delete loops in `main.py` |
| Unique constraint | `UNIQUE` column | `create_index(..., unique=True)` |
| Integrity error | `sqlalchemy.exc.IntegrityError` | `pymongo.errors.DuplicateKeyError` |
| Schema file | `Database.sql` (required) | None — collections auto-created |
| Seed data | Embedded in `Database.sql` | Run `python seed.py` once |
| Frontend (`app.js`) | Unchanged | Unchanged |
| Pydantic schemas | Unchanged | Unchanged |

---

## 🔒 Security Notes

- Never commit `.env` to Git — add it to `.gitignore`
- All `/admin/*` endpoints require a valid `admin_username` query param
- Passwords hashed with **bcrypt** via `passlib`
- OTP state is held in **process memory** — use Redis in production with multiple workers
- For production: enable HTTPS, add JWT token auth, restrict `allow_origins` in CORS
- MongoDB should be bound to `127.0.0.1` only — never expose port 27017 publicly
- Use a named Docker volume (`-v temple_data:/data/db`) so data survives container restarts

